      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, I did not provide sufficient context. The purpose of this CL is not to capture API headers. This CL attempts to fix incrementality issues in a multi-tree workspace.\n\nFor this hypothetical workflow,\n```\n$ rm rf -out\n$ multitree_build vendor/vendorimage # Step 1\n$ multitree_build vendor/vendorimage # Step 2\n```\n\nStep 2 currently regenerates the ninja file in the inner tree.\n\nThis is because `GlobHeadersForSnapshot` uses `ctx.GlobWithDeps`. This adds all the headers matching those patterns to the deps of `out/soong/build.ninja` (via `out/soong/globs/build/*`) This includes the headers for the dynamically generated `cc_api_library` module. My proposal is that we extend the ignore pattern for this globbing from `out/soong` (today) to `out/`. Then we can mount the generated `cc_api_library` Android.bp files to a subdirectory under `out/`, and this will not retrigger Soong analysis in Step 2.",
      "parentUuid": "49aed18d_784db961",
      "revId": "925cb2a82248fc9efe9948d4edeeb42910b75628",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
